6045417] [17592186490249 #edb/ref 1071 "A fair coin is flipped $5$ times. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability that the coin lands on heads at most $3$ times?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490249 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "510156d7-b5c0-5e8b-8cd5-32b7f7e0537d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490249 #edb/ref 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the coin lands on heads.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- There are $n=5$ flips.\n\n- The probability of landing heads is $p=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(5,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for the probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x}{(1-\\frac{1}{2})}^{5-x} \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that at most $3$ of the $5$ flips are heads. So, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{4} \\\\  & \\,+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =(1+5+10+10)\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5} \\\\  & =26\\cdot \\frac{1}{32} \\\\  & =0.813,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490284 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490284 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34159" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490284 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490284 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $2u+v.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490284 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a325c3ab-0a0f-53da-bbb5-9670c5e960cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490284 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply each component of $u$ by $2.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u+v & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+3 \\\\ 6+1 \\\\ 4+4 \\\\ 8+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490332 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186490390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490332 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "05a87747-f2bd-5213-af84-8786d8887033" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490332 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186490284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490334 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186490363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490334 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "07ae2f09-fe9e-5ba9-a0d7-b2c82c644d07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490334 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186311921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490344 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2ca5f55d-d481-5b90-9268-9016376d2ff8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490344 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186398347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490356 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186490332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490356 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5dd82d00-4234-54d2-a846-7b8eca37409b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490356 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186262922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490363 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186490365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218